<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mandalgarh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mandalgarh is a hill fort and town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhilwara">Bhilwara</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, on the plateau north-east of Chittor. Contested for centuries between Mewar, the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, it was one of the main strongholds of eastern Mewar. Mughal forces held it during the wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana-pratap">Maharana Pratap</a>, and with Chittor it remained outside his control at his death in 1597.</p></div>
